{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Ramakrishnan&limit=10&title=Why We Die","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"title":"Why we die ","subTitle":"the new science of aging and the quest for immortality "},{"@type":"alternative","title":"New science of aging and the quest for immortality"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Ramakrishnan, Venki,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1952-"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"marcrelator","#text":"aut"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJmhVbgTHWKBvmywRyFYfq"},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"Medical Subject Headings","#text":"Popular Work"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Popular works"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Informational works."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Documents d'information."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2024"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2024"},"issuance":"monographic","edition":"First edition."},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York, NY :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"William Morrow, an imprint of HarperCollins Publishers,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":[2024]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"310 pages : illustrations ; 24 cm."},"abstract":[{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"A groundbreaking exploration of the science of why and how we age and die-- from Nobel Prize-winning molecular biologist Venki Ramakrishnan.\"-- Provided by publisher."},{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"The knowledge of death is so terrifying that we live most of our lives in denial of it. One of the most difficult moments of childhood must be when each of us first realizes that not only we but all our loved ones will die-- and there is nothing we can do about it. Or at least, there hasn’t been. Today, we are living through a revolution in biology. Giant strides are being made in understanding why we age-- and why some species live longer than others. Could we eventually cheat disease and death and live for a very long time, possibly many times our current lifespan? Venki Ramakrishnan, recipient of the Nobel Prize in Chemistry and former president of the Royal Society, takes us on a riveting journey to the frontiers of biology, asking whether we must be mortal. Covering the recent breakthroughs in scientific research, he examines the cutting edge of efforts to extend lifespan by altering our physiology. But might death serve a necessary biological purpose? What are the social and ethical costs of attempting to live forever?\"--Front book jacket flap."}],"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Introduction -- The immortal gene and the disposable body -- Live fast and die young -- Destroying the master controller -- The problem with ends -- Resetting the biological clock -- Recycling the garbage -- Less is more -- Lessons from a lowly worm -- The stowaway within us -- Aches, pains, and vampire blood -- Crackpots or prophets? -- Should we live forever? - Acknowledgements -- Notes (pages 243-298) -- Index."},"targetAudience":{"@authority":"marctarget","#text":"adult"},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Venki Ramakrishnan."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Aging","Physiological aspects"],"genre":"Popular works"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Aging","Prevention"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Longevity"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Death"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Death (Biology)"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Death","Causes"]},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":["Aging","physiology"]},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":["Longevity","physiology"]},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Healthy Aging"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Death"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Cause of Death"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Mort (Biologie)"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Décès","Causes"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Vieillissement","Aspect physiologique"],"genre":"Ouvrages de vulgarisation"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Vieillissement","Prévention"]},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"PSYCHOLOGY / Developmental / Adulthood & Aging"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / Life Sciences / Biology"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SOCIAL SCIENCE / Death & Dying"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Death"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Death (Biology)"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Death","Causes"]},{"@authority":"sears","topic":"Death"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QP87 .R34 2024"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"WT 120 R165w 2024"},{"@edition":"23/eng/20231129","@authority":"ddc","#text":"616.07/8"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"612.67"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Why we die"},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York, NY : William Morrow, [2024]"},"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780063113299"},{"@type":"local","#text":"(DLC)  2023033371"}],"name":{"namePart":"Ramakrishnan, Venki, 1952-"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99157534708503941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"97800631132